# Do you know something about robots?
Yes, I do. Robots are becoming increasingly common nowadays, especially in industries like manufacturing, healthcare, and customer service. I’m particularly interested in how AI-powered robots can assist humans with repetitive or dangerous tasks. Although I’m not an expert, I often read articles and watch videos about new developments in robotics and artificial intelligence.

# Did you like any film that has a robot in it when you were a child?
Yes, when I was a child, I really enjoyed watching Transformers. I was fascinated by the robots because they could transform into vehicles and had unique personalities. At that age, I mainly watched it for the action scenes and special effects, but looking back, I think the movie was also quite imaginative and entertaining.

# Do you use robots in your daily life?
Not directly, but I do use some devices that are powered by robotic or AI technology in my daily life. For example, I often use smart assistants and automated applications on my phone and laptop to help with work and daily tasks. I think robots and automation are gradually becoming a part of everyday life, even if we don’t always notice it.

# Will you be comfortable if you are in a car driven by a robot?
I think I would feel a bit nervous at first because I’m still more familiar with human drivers. However, if the technology proved to be safe and reliable, I’d probably become more comfortable over time. In fact, self-driving cars could reduce human error and make transportation more convenient in the future.